WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:07.340
Opel's latest creation is the Crossland X
- a subcompact crossover.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:13.080
Part SUV, part minivan, it aims to combine
the best of both worlds - in other words,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.420
generous space inside with a fresh, cutting-edge
look.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.920
And the Crossland X certainly succeeds in
that.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.500
Car tester Emmanuel Schäfer mentions that
the strongest growth is in the B-segment,

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:25.730
or small cars.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.400
Their sales figures have doubled in the last
four years.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.090
So carmakers are scrambling to roll out new
B-segment models.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.680
Opel's contribution is the Crossland X.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.120
It resembles its somewhat bigger brother,
the Mokka X, but tones down the sportiness

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.789
and aggressive looks in favor of greater practicality
in everyday driving.

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:52.180
We test-drove the largest available engine,
the 1.2 liter turbo-gasolin with 96 kilowatts.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:58.320
It heaves the Crossland X from zero to 100
kilometers per hour in 9.1 seconds, with a

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.040
top speed of 206 kilometers per hour.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.980
Emmanuel explains that, when a carmaker introduces
a new model in a segment, they want it to

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.710
stand out from its competitors.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.900
Opel achieves this with driver assists - such
as Pedestrian Detection, which the Crossland X

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.940
is the first in its segment to offer.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:29.920
The front reveals the connection between the
Mokka and the Crossland: Opel's logo is mounted

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.420
on the grille, flanked by chrome winglets.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.500
The embedded, low-mounted fog lights emphasize
its SUV credentials.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:44.500
The visible underbody protection should do
away with any worries about scratched paint.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.720
Depending on the trim level, the colours of
the side mirrors and roof contrast

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.920
with the rest of the body.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.150
The gently sloping roof contour recalls a
minivan.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:04.660
LED tail lights are only offered with the
highest trim level, the 'Selection', as it's called.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.880
Folding down the rear seats expands the trunk
volume from 410 to 1255 liters.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.220
The interior gives a neat impression.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.440
Many of the switches are set on the steering
wheel.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:34.200
The eight-inch Touch-Infotainment system adds
at least 650 euros to the price, regardless

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.750
of the trim level.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.420
Air conditioning is standard, but automatic
climate control only comes with the Selection line.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.260
Opel is rolling out the Crossland X with a
range of five engines,

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.120
starting with the 1.2 liter gasoline engine with 60 kilowatts.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:00.520
The most powerful, though still quite fuel-efficient,
is a 1.2-liter turbo gasoline engine

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.540
with 96 kilowatts.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:11.180
Emmanuel describes the Crossland X's suspension
as offering both comfort and sportiness - though

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.310
a bit more comfort than sportiness.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.380
He forgives its slight tendency to roll - the
body sits a little higher than normal - saying

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.960
it's no problem, and the car takes curves
nimbly and swiftly.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:32.400
The Crossland X replaces the Mokka X as the
entry-level model for Opel's X range.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.240
The biggest model, the Grandland X, is on
its way.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.140
It will round off the X range at the top.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.840
Prices for the Crossland X start at just under
17,000 euros in Germany.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:50.280
But the 1.2 turbo edition we tested
will set you back at least 21,000 euros.

